\periph Source Statement|id="pubdata"
\mt1 SOURCE STATEMENT
\ip The Old Testament is eBible.org’s transcription of Sir Lancelot Charles Lee Brenton’s English Septuagint, with documented corrections to the 1870 text. The historical introductions, abbreviations, notes, and appendices are retained. The source’s Errata describes its editorial corrections; this volume is not a facsimile.
\ip The New Testament contains the 27 books of eBible.org’s KJV Cambridge Paragraph Bible (engkjvcpb). The Epistle Dedicatory follows Brenton’s 1870 introduction, then The Translators to the Reader. Closing notes remain with their NT books. The historical Cambridge title page is omitted. Scrivener’s critical introduction and scholarly appendices are absent from the digital package. Both source distributions identify their texts as public domain. eBible’s KJV notice records the continuing Crown printing rights in the United Kingdom.
\ip Source snapshots retrieved 23 September 2026 from eBible.org: eng-Brenton_usfm.zip and engkjvcpb_usfm.zip. Exact checksums and the reproducible build configuration accompany this edition.
\ip The books follow the Church of Greece’s Old Testament order, with the Prayer of Manasses after 2 Chronicles and 4 Maccabees in an Old Testament appendix. Brenton’s combined Ezra–Nehemiah is divided after chapter 10 into 2 Esdras and Nehemiah 1–13; the overlapping standalone Nehemiah source is excluded. Esther’s additions, Daniel 3’s Song of the Three Children, and Psalm 151 are retained. Susanna precedes Daniel 1 and Bel and the Dragon follows Daniel 12 as sections of Daniel. Malachias 3:19–24 is labeled 4:1–6.
\ip The source wording, notes, and references have been retained. Added words are set in regular type. Ezra–Nehemiah and Malachias chapter and verse labels are adapted as described above. The book order, title pages, section dividers, and contents belong to this edition. Brenton’s Introduction to the Apocrypha begins the historical apparatus after Revelation. Historical opinions in the apparatus belong to their original authors.
\ip Typeset with PTXprint 3.0.43, using its BSB A5 layout, Utopia, GFS Porson for Greek quotations, and Ezra SIL for Hebrew quotations. This is an English Bible; original-language passages occur only within the historical apparatus and notes.
